  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Plugin: UI Session Archive",
      "text": "[中文](README.zh.md) | English\n\nProvides **session archive management and restoration** features for the [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Harness) web interface, hiding inactive conversations from the main workspace list while keeping them accessible and restorable from a dedicated sidebar section."
    },
    {
      "section": "Target Audience and Use Cases",
      "text": "Designed for users with many active conversations who want to keep the sidebar uncluttered while preserving complete historical transcripts for later review and restoration."
    },
    {
      "section": "Key Features",
      "text": "- **One-Click Archive and Restore**: Archive sessions from the session action menu, and restore them back to their original workspaces from the sidebar footer.\n- **Pure Slot-Based Composition**: Injects seamlessly through the `sidebar.workspaces.archive` slot without leaving redundant UI artifacts when unmounted.\n- **Non-Destructive Lifecycle**: Archiving hides sessions from active grouping surfaces without altering underlying transcript logs or workspace records.\n- **Readily Accessible History**: Archived conversations can still be opened and viewed directly from the archive disclosure."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation and Quick Start",
      "text": "Install a reviewed revision into your Web profile. The repository tracks prebuilt `lib/` artifacts, so Git installation requires no local build step:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:OpenSaozi/dsh-session-archive#<commit-sha>\n```\n\nAfter installation, refresh the page to access the \"Archived (n)\" disclosure at the bottom of the sidebar."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "This plugin requires a DeepSeek Harness version whose `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-workspace` package declares the `sidebar.workspaces.archive` child slot."
    },
    {
      "section": "Storage and Privacy",
      "text": "The plugin consumes only the host-owned workspace registry archive APIs and does not store prompt text, model responses, or private credentials."
    },
    {
      "section": "What the model sees",
      "text": "Nothing. Archive and restore actions inject no `system` prompt text, messages, tool schemas, or provider request fields."
    },
    {
      "section": "Token effect",
      "text": "Zero direct tokens."
    },
    {
      "section": "KV Cache effect",
      "text": "None; archive and restore operations do not issue or alter model inference requests."
    },
    {
      "section": "Known Limitations and Deferred Work",
      "text": "- **Inspection and restoration only** — the archive disclosure focuses on history viewing and restoration, without nested session renaming actions inside the list."
    }
  ],
